    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present this substantial four-bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally positioned on one of Mount Merrion's most sought-after avenues. Although the property would benefit from modernisation, its generous proportions and excellent footprint offer a wonderful opportunity for the discerning purchaser to create an exceptional forever family home.\n\nApproached via a gravelled driveway, the property opens into a welcoming entrance hall, from which the ground-floor accommodation flows effortlessly through a series of bright and versatile reception spaces to the rear garden. To the front is an inviting living room with a large window and original tiled fireplace, opening into the study and family room, and onwards to the spacious kitchen/dining room. A sunroom with direct garden access, together with a utility room and guest WC, completes the ground floor.\n\nUpstairs, the first floor comprises three generously sized double bedrooms, a single bedroom and a well-appointed family bathroom. A spiral staircase leads to the second floor, where a large attic space provides valuable flexibility for a variety of uses.\n\nOutside, the private front driveway provides secure off-street parking for two to three cars and is framed by mature hedging. To the rear, there is a large, gravelled patio area, a raised deck overlooks the impressive westerly garden, with steps descending to an expansive lawn bordered by mature trees and hedging. Designed to make the most of the afternoon and evening sunshine, this wonderfully private outdoor space is ideal for entertaining, relaxation and children's play. There is a shed which provide useful additional storage. There is also another structure at the rear of the garden (L7.1m x W3.5m - 23ft long x 11ft wide) which can be used as a home office, gym or a teenage hangout. \n\nThe location is exceptionally convenient. The shops at The Rise, a focal point of the Mount Merrion community, are within easy walking distance, as are the community centre, churches and a wide range of sporting amenities. UCD's Belfield campus is on the doorstep, while many of south Dublin's leading schools are nearby, including Mount Anville, St Andrew's College, Blackrock College, Oatlands College, Coláiste Íosagáin, Coláiste Eoin and St Kilian's German School. Excellent transport connections include the Stillorgan Quality Bus Corridor, Aircoach, the N11 and easy access to the M50. Blackrock, Stillorgan, Merrion and Dundrum shopping centres are all within a short drive, as is the Luas Park & Ride facility at Sandyford."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.66m x 2.17m\nBright and welcoming, with a large side window and door, and timber flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 3.66m x 4.13m\nA bright, inviting reception room overlooking the front, featuring timber flooring, ceiling coving and an original tiled fireplace, with an opening to the study.\n\nStudy - 3.62m x 3.13m\nA spacious and versatile room with timber flooring and sliding doors opening to the rear garden; a door leads through to the family room.\n\nFamily Room - 3.62m x 3.17m\nA cosy reception room with timber flooring, a tiled fireplace with open fire, a window and an arched opening to the kitchen/dining room.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 7.40m x 3.50m\nA generous open-plan space with timber flooring in the dining area and tiled flooring in the kitchen. The kitchen is fitted with a good range of wall and floor units, ample worktop space, a stainless-steel sink, tiled splashback and provision for a cooker and dishwasher. A peninsula provides an ideal spot for casual dining, while glazed double doors open to the sunroom.\n\nSunroom - 3.90m x 3.50m\nA wonderfully bright, fully glazed room with timber flooring, a pine-panelled ceiling and two Velux windows. Double doors open directly onto the raised deck.\n\nUtility Room - 5.86m x 1.77m\nConveniently accessed from the kitchen, with additional storage and provision for a washing machine, making it ideal for use as a laundry room.\n\nWC - \nTiled and fitted with a WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nLanding - \nA generous landing providing access to all first-floor rooms, with a spiral staircase rising to the attic level.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.66m x 4.13m\nA spacious principal double bedroom overlooking the front, with carpet flooring and useful fitted storage beside and above the bed.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.62m x 3.53m\nA generous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.09m x 2.55m\nA well-proportioned double bedroom to the side, with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.40m x 2.17m\nA comfortable single bedroom overlooking the front.\n\nBathroom - 1.71m x 3.56m\nFully tiled and naturally bright, with two windows, a bath with overhead shower, WC, wash-hand basin with storage below and a mirrored cabinet above.\n\nAttic Room - 4.00m x 6.40m\nAccessed via a spiral staircase this is a large space with Velux windows ideal for a multitude of uses.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Substantial four-bedroom family home</li><li> Approx. 177 sq. m. / 1,905 sq. ft., including attic level</li><li> Large, private westerly rear garden 37m/121ft in length approx </li><li> Secure off-street parking for two to three cars</li><li> Prestigious Mount Merrion address</li><li> Within easy reach of leading schools and UCD</li><li> Excellent transport links to the city centre, N11 and M50</ul>"
      },
